+
+## Scene command dispatch boundary
+
+Etap 6 routes startup scene command dispatch through session-aware orchestration.
+
+The concrete dispatcher still delegates to app-owned `scene_runtime`, but hosted
+stabilization now uses `stabilize_runtime_for_session`, which sends scene commands
+through `apply_scene_command_for_session`. This keeps command lifecycle state
+visible through `SceneSessionService` while later passes move the real dispatcher
+out of `amigo-app`.
+
+## Scene clear lifecycle boundary
+
+Etap 7 records scene clearing as a first-class lifecycle phase.
+
+Runtime scene cleanup now marks `SceneSessionService` as `Clearing` before app-owned services are cleared, records `Empty` only after cleanup succeeds, and records an error if cleanup fails. A session-aware adapter exists for future call sites that already own `RuntimeSession`.
+
+## RenderSession boundary
+
+Etap 8 adds session ownership for render-frame lifecycle.
+
+`RenderSessionService` tracks render pipeline stages at session boundary:
+
+- frame extraction begin/end,
+- composition build,
+- graph build,
+- submit,
+- present,
+- last render error.
+
+`RuntimeSession` now exposes this boundary through:
+
+- `render_session_service()`
+- `begin_render_frame_extract()`
+- `complete_render_frame_extract()`
+- `complete_render_composition()`
+- `complete_render_graph_build()`
+- `complete_render_submit()`
+- `complete_render_present()`
+- `mark_render_error(...)`
